# Drafted by Gemini (side quests batch 3: mori), edited.

~ start
Narrator: Damp heather clings to the hem of an old wool coat. Above the stump, a sleek black crow watches you with one bright, yellow eye.
brother_elias [angry]: Keep your tracts and your tithes in your pockets, travelers. I hold fast to the sacred doctrine of Absolutely Nothing, and I pray to it twice before breakfast.
* Ask about his hermitage -> hermit
* Ask what the crow thinks -> crow
* Ask which faith he refuses most -> faiths
* Leave -> END

~ hermit
brother_elias [sly]: A leaky pine lean-to is temple enough for a mind swept clean of superstition. Though if the butcher's wife leaves salted pork by my stone, I am no fanatic to let it spoil.
-> start

~ crow
crow [neutral]: Caw.
brother_elias [angry]: Hold your tongue, you feathered deacon! He claims I bowed my head when the thunder cracked last night, when I was merely looking for my spectacles.
-> start

~ faiths
brother_elias [weary]: The Old Ways smell of wet bark, the Patient Lady waters weeds, and those Brightsingers chirp until a man's ears bleed.
brother_elias [angry]: Worst are the fools carving antlers on hares in the dark, as if a rabbit did not have trouble enough getting down its hole.
-> start
